A wrong submission rejects the whole hypothesis, not just one guessed cell. Re-derive from all demo pairs rather than iterating local edits. In cluttered inputs, identify regular object geometry and compare each output cell: isolated cells of other colors within otherwise uniform shapes may be noise or overlays, and the output may normalize the whole object while removing those intrusions. Conversely, do not generalize this without demo support. Audit both the transformed extent and every unusual cell outside it; test the candidate against every demo before spending another attempt.

